        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Louis XIV</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">1638 CE – 1715 CE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Born</span><span class="info-stat-val">5 September 1638 at the Château de Saint-Germain-en-Laye, as Louis Dieudonné; son of Louis XIII and Anne of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>, of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-bourbon">House of Bourbon</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Died</span><span class="info-stat-val">1 September 1715 at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/versailles">Versailles</a>, of gangrene, four days before his 77th birthday; buried in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basilica-of-saint-denis">Basilica of Saint-Denis</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Who they were</span><span class="info-stat-val">King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> from 14 May 1643 until his death in 1715; under the regency of his mother Anne of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> and the chief minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jules-mazarin">Cardinal Mazarin</a> until 1661, then ruling without a chief minister</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">the longest reign of any monarch; the consolidation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/absolute-monarchy">absolute monarchy</a>; the palace of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/versailles">Versailles</a> and its court; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franco-dutch-war">Franco-Dutch War</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nine-years-war">Nine Years' War</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-spanish-succession">War of the Spanish Succession</a>; the revocation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edict-of-nantes">Edict of Nantes</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jean-baptiste-colbert">Colbert</a>'s financial and commercial reforms; patronage of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moliere">Molière</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jean-racine">Racine</a>, Lully and Le Brun</span></div>
